Controller credential decryption refusal

Nine controller credential helpers now raise a fixed ValueError when a value recognized as encrypted cannot be decrypted. They no longer return that encrypted value as a password, OAuth secret or API token. Legacy plaintext, Unicode plaintext, empty inputs and readable encrypted credentials retain their existing behavior. RADIUS now recognizes plaintext before attempting decryption.

Affected callers include the shared adapter factory; UniFi fallback construction; PoE, switch, access-point and network adapter construction; RADIUS, roaming and VPN orchestration. Constructor checks ensure corrupt recognized credentials fail before construction. The real Controller ORM already rejects corrupt password and cloud-secret properties; those guards are unchanged and explicitly controlled. Its config.token_secret is a separate path: the native PostgreSQL/TLS probe confirms the previous helper forwarded unreadable ciphertext as an API token and the corrected helper refuses before a request.

A first native probe incorrectly expected the already-protected ORM password path to send ciphertext. That failed attempt is retained, and the corrected probe exercises the real unguarded token path without removing existing guards. Synthetic appliance responses and event/deep-sync edges do not establish hardware acceptance.

This is not a credential migration, key rotation or storage-format change. The existing Fernet-recognition heuristic remains unchanged; strings not recognized as encrypted retain legacy plaintext semantics. In particular, malformed/truncated values that do not match that heuristic are not newly classified here. Failed reads are surfaced; no stored credentials are rewritten.

Local qualification:86 new tests (39 original regressions and47 controls),1062 related PostgreSQL-backed tests, and28 before/after PostgreSQL/TLS cases. A backend-only agent-source test remains an explicit original skip and is checked separately in the assembled agent contract; it is not relabeled as a pass. Fresh frozen-source and shipping-image gates remain required.
